---
// /story/ became part of /about/ on 2026-10-21, when the top bar was simplified (tracker pattern rule 4.21).
// A plain redirect would drop the part of an old link after "#" (one entry of the story), so this page
// keeps it: /story/#x goes to /about/#x, and /story/ alone to /about/#story. Without scripts, the refresh
// and the link still reach the right part of the page.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>Moved to About · Outrunning Ageing</title>
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://outrunningageing.com/about/#story" />
    <script is:inline>location.replace('/about/' + (location.hash || '#story'));</script>
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0;url=/about/#story" />
  </head>
  <body><a href="/about/#story">This page is now part of About.</a></body>
</html>
